LispView library version of xloadimage: libxloadimage.a

I've made some minor changes to xloadimage so that it can be used as 
a C library.  The library, libxloadimage.a,  is used by LispView to 
read image files, it depends on the functions loadImage, freeImage, a
truncated version of sendImagetoX, and the structures: RGBMap and Image.
The Makefile Makefile.lispview should be used to recompile the sources
and build the library - libxloadimage.a.  The library does not contain 
all of the objects that are linked into the xloadimage program.


The changes I've made are itemized below.

- imagetypes.h 
Changed ImageTypes table, now only includes support for Sun
Pixrect/Icon and Raster files, X11 bitmap, pixmap, and window dump
files, and portable bitmap format.  This change cuts the size of the 
library by about half.  Since the other formats can all be converted
to PBM format this change should be liveable.  If not, it's easy enough
to change imagetypes.h and build a new version of the library.


- imagetypes.c 
Added ";;;" prefix to messages printed by loadImage


- sunraster.c 
Changed babble function - preceeds message with ";;;"

Changed calls to exit in sunRasterLoad to EXIT_SUNRASTERLOAD.

Changed calls to exit in sunRead to EXIT_SUNREAD, sunread is an 
int function (was void)


- xbitmap.c 
Changed single call to exit to (badFile) to 
{freeImage(image); zclose(zf); return( (Image *)0 );}

Changed babble code - preceed message with ";;;"


- send.c => lv-send.c
New version for LispView called lv-send.c.  The new version doesn't attempt
to compress the colormap and like all of the other modules it doesn't call exit
(anymore).  


xpixmap.c
xwd.c
zio.c
new.c


- sunicon.c 
This is new.  It has the same constraints as the XView version, 
libxvol/icon/icon_load.c and, unlike most of the other modules,
it doesn't automatically uncompress it's input (id doesn't use the zio
input module).  It's unlikely anyone will ever notice.


The following files aren't used at the moment but they have been modified:

g3.c - doesn't call exit (unless compiled with -DALLOW_G3_ERRORS)
cmuwmraster.c  - calls to exit replaced with EXIT_CMUWMLOAD
faces.c - calls to exit replaced with EXIT_FACESLOAD
fbm.c - single call to exit in fbmLoad replaced with return( (Image *)0 ); /* exit(1); */



